# tok — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the keys you need. `tok` does NOT
# auto-load `.env` — export the variables yourself (e.g. via `set -a; source .env; set +a`)
# or rely on your shell/tool of choice.

# --- Anthropic (Claude) -------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED for any `tok anthropic/<model>` invocation. There is no public
# Claude tokenizer, so every Anthropic count goes through the remote
# Messages.CountTokens API. Without this key, the CLI prints an error and
# exits 1.
# Get one: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Google (Gemini) ----------------------------------------------------------
# RARELY needed. As of v1.2.0, every model in the built-in Gemini catalog
# tokenizes locally — directly via google.golang.org/genai/tokenizer for
# 1.5/2.0/2.5/3-pro-preview, and via the gemma3 alias fallback in
# internal/provider/google.go for the 3.x preview names that the SDK does
# not yet list (gemini-3.1-pro-preview, gemini-3-flash-preview,
# gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview).
#
# Set this only if you want to count tokens for a brand-new Gemini model
# whose name matches NEITHER the SDK's table NOR the alias map. Either
# GEMINI_API_KEY or GOOGLE_API_KEY works; if both are set, GOOGLE_API_KEY
# takes precedence (mirrors the genai SDK's own rule).
# Get one: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- HuggingFace --------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL for public models. REQUIRED for private models, and recommended
# to avoid HuggingFace API rate-limits during autocomplete (`<org>/<TAB>`).
# Get one: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
HF_TOKEN=

# --- OpenAI -------------------------------------------------------------------
# RARELY needed. As of v1.2.0, every model in the built-in OpenAI catalog
# tokenizes locally — directly via tiktoken-go where the model is known,
# and via the o200k_base / cl100k_base prefix fallback in
# internal/provider/openai.go for the 5.1/5.2/5.4/5.5 series and other new
# names tiktoken-go doesn't yet list.
#
# Set this only if you want to count tokens for a brand-new OpenAI model
# whose name matches NEITHER tiktoken-go NOR the prefix rules
# (gpt-5*/gpt-4o*/gpt-4.1*/gpt-4*/gpt-3.5*/o1*/o3*/o4*). The remote
# fallback uses POST /v1/responses/input_tokens.
# Get one: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
